# The image needs the source and the lock file, nothing else.
#
# Unlike .gitignore, .dockerignore patterns are anchored at the build-context
# root: `__pycache__/` matches the root directory only and lets `app/__pycache__/`
# into the image, so every pattern that has to match at any depth carries the
# `**/` prefix (`**/` also matches zero directories, so the root is covered).
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/

# The image's Python comes from its base image tag, not from a local pin.
.python-version

# The tests run outside the image.
**/tests/

# Local data and secrets must never enter a build context.
**/uploads/
**/data/
**/*.db
**/*.sqlite3
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/.DS_Store
